<title>POLAND: NFI Fund 12 has 32.9 pct of Prochnik.</title>
<headline>NFI Fund 12 has 32.9 pct of Prochnik.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 12th National Investment Fund (NFI) in Poland's mass privatisation programme has 493,500 shares, or 32.9 percent, of textile firm Prochnik SA, the company said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>In February the 12th NFI Fund announced a public tender offer to buy Prochnik shares at 11 zlotys per share during which the fund bought 343,501 shares.</p>
<p>It earlier bought 9.9 percent of Prochnik shares from administrators of bankrupt Westa SA insurer.</p>
<p>On Wednesday Prochnik traded at 9.95 zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
